id: pm-csv-9y0w
title: Keep toolchain acceptance aligned with built-in merge drivers and shipped history
description: "Repair Dependabot PR #170. The earlier assertion expected Git built-in merge=text in local driver registrations after pm-cli GH-1460; the branch already filters built-ins. The supplied job now passes all 283 tests and fails changelog:check because pm-changelog 2026.10.14 preserves a reopened item's original shipped entry. Add behavioral negative controls, regenerate the changelog, and certify the dependency branch with both release gates."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[2]: regression,toolchain
created_at: "2026-10-20T08:16:10.887Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-20T08:41:59.141Z"
author: codex-agent
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: Both full release gates pass at unchanged thresholds; regression controls fail with the driver filter or generated changelog reverted; original Dependabot branch is pushed without merging.
comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-20T08:16:51.360Z",codex-agent,"Classification: intended upstream changes with stale consumer acceptance artifacts. pm-cli CHANGELOG 2026.10.14 GH-1460 (https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/v2026.10.15/CHANGELOG.md) declares extension assets with Git's built-in text driver; only custom drivers require local registration. Existing branch commit 1da775a filters those names. Supplied job 118228111725 passes 283/283 and first exits nonzero at changelog:check. pm-changelog CHANGELOG 2026.10.14 (https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/blob/v2026.10.16/CHANGELOG.md) intentionally preserves shipped entries after reopen/close, restoring the original pm-csv-yriu entry under 2026.9.6 alongside its later 2026.9.7 completion. Plan: exercise all three Git built-ins with real Git, assert both shipped entries, regenerate tracked output, prove negative controls, then run isolated npm and Bun release gates. origin/main is already an ancestor; draft state remains false."
  "2026-10-20T08:17:29.906Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof: node --test --test-name-pattern='Git resolves text' test/prepare-merge-driver.test.ts exits 1 with only customDrivers filtering reverted to return all declared drivers: expected local registrations then wrongly include binary/text/union, while real Git resolves all three without them. Restored filter: focused suite 11/11 passes. Independently restored only HEAD:CHANGELOG.md, leaving tests unchanged: node --test test/shipped-changelog.test.ts exits 1 because the 2026.9.6 original shipped entry is absent. Restored generated CHANGELOG.md; both shipped completions pass. These are consumer acceptance/artifact defects exposed by intended upstream behavior; no upstream rollback or history rewrite."
  "2026-10-20T08:30:39.985Z",codex-agent,"Full npm gate passed: env HOME=<temporary-home> GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 npm run release:check. Node 24.19.0/npm 11.17.0: 285 tests passed; failures/cancelled/skipped/todo all zero; measured lines/branches/functions all 100 percent across the unchanged three-source scope. Packed acceptance passed npm-current, bun-current, and npm-minimum (3/3), plus production audit, docstrings, duplicate gate, changelog check, attestation and release-date verification. Full Bun gate is running next on unchanged code. Linked regression run also passed 11/11; pm reports tracking_disabled, so results are recorded here."
  "2026-10-20T08:41:00.086Z",codex-agent,"Full Bun gate passed: env HOME=<temporary-home> GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 bun run release:check (Bun 1.3.5), same code as npm. 285/285 tests; zero failures/cancelled/skipped/todo; 100 percent measured lines/branches/functions; 3/3 packed consumers; all static, audit, changelog and release verification stages passed. No thresholds changed. Both negative controls are restored. Item remains in_progress for orchestrator verification; claim released before commit."
  "2026-10-20T08:41:59.141Z",codex-agent,"Additional read-only checks: pm validate reports ok=true with existing advisory metadata/trust warnings. Strict health reports pm-github host-version skew (development host 2026.10.15 versus installed extension host 2026.10.19), plus stale-item advisories. This is separate from the passing release gates and is tracked as an out-of-scope follow-up; no extension or telemetry configuration changed."
